  "about": "Wire v10 stream frames (ikigai-wire, ledger #2242), computed by crates/ikigai-wire/tests/stream_vectors.rs, which fails if this file differs from what the codec writes. Hex is lowercase. `payload` is a frame's bytes; `framed` adds the u32 big-endian length every frame carries on the IPC socket and on a QUIC stream of frames (which opens with `stream_magic`). Tags 6 to 9 are the same in both directions: head, chunk (a varint length, then the bytes, at most `max_chunk`), end, abort (a WireError). A body is whole only at END; a stream that stops without it is a failure, never a shorter body. Each abort is named by its error's failure class.",
